CM_ BO_ 80 "BMS charger command. B4-B5=suspected rolling counter/validation (charger throttles to ~6A when non-baseline; frame likely rejected). B6-B7=unknown. BMS Charger Sys Main Current not cleanly decoded -- may be measured (not commanded) or in B6-B7.";
CM_ BO_ 469 "HV-to-14V converter status. Source: DCDC hardware manual.";
CM_ BO_ 471 "BMS command to DCDC converter. Source: DCDC hardware manual.";
CM_ BO_ 624 "BMS fault status. B0 high nibble=BMSFaultSeverity (0=No Fault, 1-6 progressively severe), low nibble=BMSFaultCode. VICD: BMS_Recvd 0x270, handler 0x15EF. B6/B7 active but unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 625 "GWM VehFaults relay on B CAN (1 frame after 0x270 BMS source). B0=fault severity + lamp request + test flag. B1-B4=VehicleFault (32-bit fault code).";
CM_ SG_ 625 VehFaultSeverity "Encoding 0-6 same as 0x270 BMSFaultSeverity.";
CM_ SG_ 625 VehicleFaultLampReq "0=OFF, 1=YELLOW, 2=RED, 3=INVALID.";
CM_ SG_ 625 VehicleFaultB0Bit2 "Set during key-on lamp test and briefly at drive end. NOT set during active faults -- lamp-test-active flag.";
CM_ BO_ 628 "LabVIEW: ChrgrSysFaultsTemp (CMM_glb.xml). Signals: ChrgrFaults_0..5 (uint16+uint8) + Chrgr1Temp, Chrgr2Temp (uint8). Byte-level encoding unconfirmed -- LabVIEW cluster exceeds 8 bytes when packed sequentially.";
CM_ BO_ 629 "BMS battery power limits and measurements. B0=BattSentDischargeLimit/MotorDriveLimit (CODACAN alias, same byte). B1=BattSentChargeLimit. B2-B3=PackCurrent. B4-B5=PackVoltage. B6=BattSentHVACLimits. B7=unidentified, possibly 4th current limit. Note: B4 always=1 in normal LFP operation (pack voltage 312-380V keeps uint16 MSB=1) -- prior 'HVActive' label was a misidentification.";
CM_ SG_ 629 BattSentDischargeLimit "CODACAN alias: MotorDriveLimit.";
CM_ SG_ 629 PackCurrent "Positive = charging.";
CM_ SG_ 629 PackVoltage "B4=0 is a sentinel (triggers ~4V display); normal LFP operation keeps B4=1.";
CM_ BO_ 630 "HVAC power/thermal status. 10 Hz. Sender: HVAC ECU. B0=PTC power, B1=ACCM power, B2=HV disable status (sub-byte layout unresolved), B3=coolant outlet temp, B4=PTC outlet temp, B5=PTC heater PWM, B6=radiator fan PWM, B7=batt cooling fan PWM. PWM signals use open-drain hardware; CODACAN 'Inverted' label = wire polarity only, not CAN encoding.";
CM_ SG_ 630 HVACHVDisableStatus "PROVISIONAL encoding: 0=Invalid, 2=enum-3 (no label), 5=All HV Components disabled, 8=All HV Components not disabled. Sub-byte bit layout unresolved.";
CM_ BO_ 631 "CMM (master charger module) temperatures.";
CM_ BO_ 633 "CMM charger output measurements. HVOutVoltage matches pack voltage from C CAN.";
CM_ BO_ 634 "CMS (slave charger module) temperatures. Same Lear OBC hardware as CMM.";
CM_ BO_ 635 "CMS charger input measurements. Same Lear OBC hardware as CMM.";
CM_ BO_ 636 "CMS charger output measurements. CMS is the slave charger module; CMM is master.";
CM_ BO_ 637 "CMM (master charger module) input measurements.";
CM_ BO_ 705 "BMS driving range estimates. B0=StatusByte (flips all readings at raw=0x70, likely health/CRC). B1=DrivingRange_Exp, B3=DrivingRange_Max, B5=DrivingRange_Min. B2/B4/B6=0x00 padding. All range signals provisional -- scales ~1.1-1.17, units likely miles.";
CM_ SG_ 705 DrivingRange_Exp "PROVISIONAL: scale unconfirmed, units likely miles.";
CM_ SG_ 705 DrivingRange_Max "PROVISIONAL: scale unconfirmed, units likely miles.";
CM_ SG_ 705 DrivingRange_Min "PROVISIONAL: scale unconfirmed, units likely miles.";
CM_ BO_ 888 "BMS mode and network management. B0[7:4]=HVPowermode, B0[3:0]=Chargemode, B1[1:0]=KeepWakeNetworkBMS, B1[2]=rolling counter, B1[7:3]=always 0, B2=BMSmode. B3-B7 unused.";
CM_ SG_ 888 HVPowermode "0=Invalid, 2=HV Off Imminent, 3=HV On Drive (provisional), 4=HV On Drive, 5=HV On Charge, 6=HV On Support (provisional), 7=HV On Support (provisional). Values 8-F show as raw numerics in CODACAN.";
CM_ SG_ 888 Chargemode "0=Invalid, 1=No Prox, 2=Prox Present (open/wait), 3=Charging, 4=Charge Complete (provisional), 5=Maintenance Charging (provisional), 6=Invalid, 15=Invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 888 KeepWakeNetworkBMS "Bit0=0 -> Network Alive Request, bit0=1 -> No Network Request. Bit1 is don't-care.";
CM_ SG_ 888 B1_Counter "1-bit rolling counter, toggles every frame at ~6Hz.";
CM_ SG_ 888 B1_high "B1[7:3] 5-bit field. Always 0 in available captures. Purpose unknown (possible counter or reserved).";
CM_ BO_ 897 "BMS cell voltage extremes. B0-B1=min, B2-B3=max, B4-B5=avg. OV cutoff at 3750 mV. B6=VminId, B7=VmaxId (cell indices).";
CM_ SG_ 897 MinCellVoltage "104-cell LFP pack.";
CM_ SG_ 897 MaxCellVoltage "OV cutoff at 3750 mV.";
CM_ SG_ 897 VminId "0-based index.";
CM_ SG_ 897 VmaxId "0-based index.";
CM_ BO_ 898 "BMS cell temperature stats. B0=Cell_T_avg, B1=Cell_T_max (provisional), B2=Cell_T_min (provisional), B3=MaxTempId, B4=MinTempId.";
CM_ SG_ 898 Cell_T_avg "Invalid sentinels: 0x00 (standby), 0x33 (charge stopped).";
CM_ SG_ 898 Cell_T_max "PROVISIONAL.";
CM_ SG_ 898 Cell_T_min "PROVISIONAL.";
CM_ BO_ 899 "BMS battery status. B0-B1=SoC. B2=packed boolean flags (see signals). B3-B7 unknown. PROVISIONAL: B2 bit2/bit1 (HVBattCharging/ChrgPortOpen) assignment may be swapped.";
CM_ SG_ 899 HVBattCharging "PROVISIONAL: may swap identity with ChrgPortOpen (B2 bit1).";
CM_ SG_ 899 ChrgPortOpen "PROVISIONAL: may swap identity with HVBattCharging (B2 bit2). Toggles rapidly at session start (~0.3s period), consistent with J1772 handshake.";
CM_ SG_ 899 B2_bit7 "Always 0 in available data. Possibly LowSOC, HVBattOverheat, or HVBattMalfunc.";
CM_ SG_ 899 B2_bit0 "Always 0 in available data. Possibly J772Activity (J1772 pilot signal active).";
CM_ BO_ 912 "BMS HV battery temperature zone sensors. B0=FrontInletAirTemp, B1=RearInletAirTemp, B2=ReturnAirTempPsg, B3=ReturnAirTempDrv, B4=AllowedCellTempMax, B5=AllowedCellTempMin, B6=AllowedCellTempDiff (non-negative delta, no offset), B7=AllowedHumidity (scale TBD). Sender: BMS.";
CM_ SG_ 912 AllowedCellTempDiff "Non-negative temperature delta (no offset, unlike other temp signals).";
CM_ SG_ 912 AllowedHumidity "PROVISIONAL: scale TBD.";
CM_ BO_ 913 "HVAC ambient air state. B0=UnderHoodHumidity, B1=UnderHoodTemp, B2=OpAirHumidity, B3=OPAirTemp, B4=ReturnAirTemp, B5=EvapAirOffTemp (not in original CODACAN field list). B6-B7 inactive. Sender: HVAC ECU. Humidity signals may be marked Inverted in CODACAN -- verify direction against real data.";
CM_ SG_ 913 OPAirTemp "Outside/ambient air temperature.";
CM_ BO_ 1040 "AC compressor command. Ford AM64-19D623-AB electric scroll compressor. B0=raw command byte (boolean signals observed but bit assignments unresolved).";
CM_ SG_ 1040 compressor_on_off "~360ms latency before status reports Running.";
CM_ SG_ 1040 target_compressor_speed "Hardware max 6000 rpm.";
CM_ SG_ 1040 max_pwr_consumption "Hardware max 4.5 kW.";
CM_ BO_ 1081 "AC compressor status feedback. 10 Hz.";
CM_ SG_ 1081 COMPRESSOR_STATUS "0=Standby (HV available, no run cmd), 1=Running, 2=CASS Complete (self-test/startup sequence complete), 3=Off (no HV or shutdown).";
CM_ BO_ 1162 "DCDC secondary status with temperatures. Source: DCDC hardware manual.";
CM_ BO_ 1557 "LabVIEW: ChrgrSysLimits (CMM_glb.xml). Float signals likely use div32 encoding -- shown as 8-bit placeholder, scale tentative.";
CM_ BO_ 1558 "LabVIEW: ChrgrSysCtrlEcho (CMM_glb.xml). Echo of charger control commands. Encoding tentative.";
CM_ BO_ 1559 "Charger system bus measurements. B2=unknown (always 0x00; may be MSB of ChrgrSysBusCurrent uint16). B4=status flags (0x83/0x84, bit0 toggles). B5=0x00. B6=bimodal 0x00/0x1F transient. B7=0x00. LabVIEW names B4-5=ChrgrSys12VSysVoltage, B6-7=ChrgrSys12VSysCurrent but observed values do not match div32.";
CM_ BO_ 1568 "VICD: BMS_Recvd 0x620. Sparse decode, cluster unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 1834 "VICD: BMS_Recvd 0x72A. Simple byte copy, cluster unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 928 "SRS airbag module + seatbelt switch status. B CAN only, 10 Hz. B0: SRS status bits + seatbelt warning. B1: buckle switches.";
CM_ SG_ 928 SRS_ModuleActive "Set in both normal and fault conditions.";
CM_ SG_ 928 SRS_FaultFlag "Active when SRS DTC present (e.g. B1382/B2505 in parts car).";
CM_ SG_ 928 SeatbeltWarning "B0.bit3. 1=warning active. Cleared when driver buckles. Medium confidence -- needs test with occupied passenger seat to confirm combined vs driver-only semantics.";
CM_ SG_ 928 DriverBuckle "B1.bit4. 1=unbuckled, 0=buckled. HIGH confidence.";
CM_ SG_ 928 PassengerBuckle "B1.bit2. 1=unbuckled, 0=buckled. HIGH confidence. Test used unoccupied passenger seat -- driver reached over to buckle it.";
CM_ BO_ 1169 "IPK instrument cluster fault lamp status on B CAN. B0 is a key-on latch -- set once at key-on, does NOT change during lamp test or mid-drive faults. B0 bits 2-0=fault lamp indicators. B0 bit 3=IPK_B0_Active. B1 bits 4,3,1 set in normal but cleared with active faults -- encoding unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 1169 IPK_FaultLamps "Which bit maps to which module (ABS/SRS/HVAC) is unresolved.";
CM_ BO_ 1170 "UNKNOWN: 0x492. All zeros in parts car dataset. Possible IPK echo or secondary status frame.";
CM_ BO_ 1786 "GWM broadcasts VIN on B CAN at 10 Hz as a 3-frame sequence. B0=VIN_FrameCounter (0/1/2); B1-B7=7 ASCII chars per frame. Frame 0: chars 1-7; Frame 1: chars 8-14; Frame 2: chars 15-17 + padding. Same ID rebroadcast on D CAN.";
CM_ SG_ 1786 VIN_Frame "Each byte B1-B7 is one raw ASCII character of the VIN.";

VAL_ 888 HVPowermode 0 "Invalid" 2 "HV Off Imminent" 3 "HV On Drive" 4 "HV On Drive" 5 "HV On Charge" 6 "HV On Support" 7 "HV On Support" ;
VAL_ 888 Chargemode 0 "Invalid" 1 "No Prox" 2 "Prox Present Open Wait Active" 3 "Charging" 4 "Charge Complete" 5 "Maintenance Charging" 6 "Invalid" 15 "Invalid" ;
VAL_ 888 KeepWakeNetworkBMS 0 "Network Alive Request" 1 "No Network Request" 2 "Network Alive Request" 3 "No Network Request" ;
VAL_ 1081 COMPRESSOR_STATUS 0 "Standby" 1 "Running" 2 "CASS Complete" 3 "Off" ;
VAL_ 624 BMSFaultSeverity 0 "No Fault" 1 "Information Only, No Limiting" 2 "Minor Performance Limiting" 3 "Limited Performance" 4 "Heavily Limited Performance, Contactors Will Not Close" 5 "Heavily Limited Performance, Operation Should Be Stopped" 6 "ALL HV Components Should Be Disabled, BMS Will Open" 7 "Reserved" 8 "Reserved" 9 "Reserved" 10 "Reserved" 11 "Reserved" 12 "Reserved" 13 "Reserved" 14 "Reserved" 15 "Reserved" ;

